# The only effective .dockerignore in this repository. Both images build with
# the repository root as their context (`context: .` in the Compose files and
# CI, `docker build ... .` in the Makefile), so Docker consults this file and
# nothing else. There used to be a backend/.dockerignore and a
# frontend/.dockerignore; neither was ever read, and neither excluded .env*,
# which made the build context look filtered per stack when it was not.
.git
.github
# Environment configuration never belongs in a build context. Cover both the
# root Compose file and nested framework variants such as frontend/.env.local.
.env*
**/.env*
*.env
**/*.env
.venv
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/htmlcov
**/coverage.xml
**/*.db
docs/assets
